course: dictionary
lesson: 16034
title: Checking that something is true
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Verification is a formal word, but it is simple: it means checking that something is true, correct or real. When you check your work, you are doing verification. «Before we share the results, we need verification that the numbers are correct.» The sentence tells you someone must check the numbers, so verification must mean checking.
explain: In maths, one way to get verification is to use the opposite (inverse) operation. «Sam checked 56 ÷ 7 = 8 by doing 8 × 7, which gave 56.» Multiplying back to the start shows that the division was right. Always ask: how can I prove this is correct?
explain: On a computer, verification can mean checking that you really are who you say you are. «To log in, Mia had to type the code sent to her phone.» The code is verification that Mia is really Mia and not someone pretending to be her. Two-step verification means you need two checks, such as a password and a code.
fact: Verification means checking that something is true, correct or real.
fact: Verification is a noun, and it is usually uncountable, so we say «some verification», not «a verification».
fact: In maths, checking your answer with the inverse operation is one kind of verification.
fact: In science, repeating an experiment helps give verification of a result.
fact: On computers, verification can be a code sent to your phone to show you are really who you say you are.
exercise: «The scientists repeated the experiment to get verification of their result.» What does verification mean here? | Forgetting the result | *Checking that the result is true | Making the experiment louder | Painting the lab walls
exercise: Sam checked 56 ÷ 7 = 8 by doing 8 × 7. What kind of check is this? | A guess | *Verification of the answer | A picture | A new question
exercise: «Mia typed the code sent to her phone.» What is the code for? | Choosing a colour | *Verification that she is really Mia | Making her phone faster | Buying a game
test: «Please provide ___ of your result.» Which word fits the gap? | sandwich | whistle | holiday | *verification
test: Two-step verification sends a code to your phone. What is its job? | To give you a free game | To make your phone ring | To delete your photos | *To check you really are who you say you are
exam: «The teacher asked for verification that the answer was correct.» Which description is best? | A type of food | A loud noise | A new word for a question | *A check that something is true, correct or real
